# Build context for deploy/cloudflare/container/Dockerfile.
#
# Later rules win, so the order below is load-bearing: broad excludes first,
# then the two things inside .dsh that the image genuinely needs, then the one
# directory that must stay out even though it sits under them.

# ── installed for THIS platform ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The image runs its own `npm install` for linux/amd64 before the wildcard copy.
# Copying a Windows tree over it replaces working binaries with ones that cannot
# execute — and does it silently, because the paths all still exist.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# ── the professor's own home ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .dsh holds .credentials.yaml, the key the Models page writes, and every
# session transcript on this machine. An image is distributed to Cloudflare's
# network and started for every professor, so none of that may be in it.
.dsh/**

# Except the composition, which is not state and which deploy/dsh-user mirrors
# out of the checkout on every boot. Leave these out and the harness boots
# without the professor preset — the standard coding agent answers instead, and
# nothing reports it as wrong.
!.dsh/profiles/sample/**
!.dsh/.agent-presets/**

# But not the link farm the harness writes into the profile on first boot. It is
# rebuilt per container, it is several hundred entries, and on Windows these are
# junctions that do not survive a copy into a Linux image as anything useful.
.dsh/profiles/node_modules/

# ── the API key, by the other route it can live at ──────────────────────────
.env
.env.local

# ── not needed to run ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitattributes
workspace/
*.log
.DS_Store
